# What: Sample HTTP requests for the outbox-events sample (VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP client).
# Why: [CAP-M18] watch the outbox at work: confirm an order, then see invoice and booking appear.
# If missing or unlinked: Learners have to reconstruct the URLs from the tests.
#
# Start first: npm run watch - the log shows the queued messages being processed.

@P = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/orders

### 1 Orders
GET {{P}}/Orders

### 2 Confirm an order: status change, message and shipment booking in one transaction
POST {{P}}/Orders(f1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001)/OrderService.confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3 Invoice written by the consumer of OrderService.OrderConfirmed (after commit)
GET {{P}}/Invoices

### 4 Booking written by the queued ShippingService call
GET {{P}}/ShipmentBookings

### 5 Confirm twice -> 409, no second message
POST {{P}}/Orders(f1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001)/OrderService.confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{}
